{"expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations", "id": "10476", "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10476", "key": "AIN-153", "fields": {"description": {"type": "doc", "version": 1, "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "As an application user, I want consistent, readable colors and shared components across the application so that navigation, actions and states feel coherent in light and dark modes."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "User-approved palette: Espresso #38271F; Terracotta #D66A42; Sand #F2DDBB; Dusty Sage #A9BAA0; Porcelain #F6F0E8. EnsuredXDS owns color definitions, derived accessible tones and reusable visual components."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Acceptance: central light/dark semantic tokens and generated CSS defaults; migrate application-local colors and shared component styling to XDS; cover host UI, Marketplace, Network, registration/auth, SubmissionUI, Logistics and service catalog; preserve payloads and workflows; verify contrast, focus, hover, disabled, validation and theme persistence with executable Storybook interactions and relevant builds. Record remaining gaps explicitly. Local runtime refresh is included; production deployment/package publication is not authorized."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Dependencies: central tokens precede consumer migration, then verification. AIN-150 is a completed Settings regression boundary; AIN-151 is a pre-existing API-boundary issue unrelated to palette acceptance; AIN-87 is independent document workflow work. Broader AIN-1 release acceptance remains separate and incomplete."}]}]}, "issuelinks": [], "subtasks": [{"id": "10477", "key": "AIN-154", "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10477", "fields": {"summary": "[Palette] Define Espresso palette and shared theme con